# KS visual hash catalog remediation governance

When editing KS visual surfaces, generated HTML, design catalog files, visual audit tooling, or website UX remediation plans:

- Every visible reusable page/layout/section/component/primitive/style/diagram/interaction/desktop interface must be represented in `docs/design/catalog/visual-registry.yaml` or explicitly family-covered.
- Every emitted visual root should include both `hash="XYZ"` and `data-ks-hash="XYZ"`, with three ASCII letters and global uniqueness.
- Visual implementation changes must update the relevant design contract unless the change is explicitly marked `no_visual_change` with evidence.
- Do not leave design contracts with unresolved placeholder language.
- Do not make `analyze-website-ux.mjs` call `score-website-ux.mjs`, or vice versa.
- Do not add runtime dependency from the website UX auditor/scorer to the design-catalog YAML parser. Use generated JSON or shared dependency-free helpers.
- For public consumer sites, do not claim hash deployment until raw HTML is checked for `hash="XYZ"` and `data-ks-hash="XYZ"`.
- Final reports must use current generated counts, not stale copied numbers.
